<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=93=96 Com=
binations - When Order Doesn't Matter</h3>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=8C=B1 Ngu=E1=BB=
=93n G=E1=BB=91c &amp; Motivation</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">T=E1=BA=A1i Figma, ch=C3=BAng t=
=C3=B4i face m=E1=BB=99t interesting problem: users c=C3=B3 th=E1=BB=83 sel=
ect multiple design elements simultaneously =C4=91=E1=BB=83 apply bulk oper=
ations. V=E1=BB=9Bi 50 elements tr=C3=AAn canvas, c=C3=B3 bao nhi=C3=AAu di=
fferent ways users c=C3=B3 th=E1=BB=83 select exactly 5 elements cho group =
operation?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=C4=90=C3=A2y l=C3=A0 combinatio=
n problem - we care v=E1=BB=81 which elements =C4=91=C6=B0=E1=BB=A3c select=
ed, but not v=E1=BB=81 order c=E1=BB=A7a selection.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Problem Statement Chi Ti=
=E1=BA=BFt:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Combinations critical trong soft=
ware engineering cho:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Feature Selection</stro=
ng>: Which features to include trong release?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Resource Allocation</st=
rong>: Which servers to assign cho specific workloads?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Testing Strategy</stron=
g>: Which test cases combinations =C4=91=E1=BB=83 cover scenarios?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>User Interface</strong>=
: Which elements user can select simultaneously?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>A/B Testing</strong>: W=
hich user segments =C4=91=E1=BB=83 test feature variations?</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Key difference t=E1=BB=AB permut=
ations: <strong>order is irrelevant</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Selecting [A, B, C] same as sel=
ecting [C, A, B]</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">We care about the set of items,=
 not the sequence</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Typically used cho selection, g=
rouping, v=C3=A0 sampling problems</li>
</ul>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">=F0=9F=94=AC B=E1=BA=
=A3n Ch=E1=BA=A5t &amp; Mechanism</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Core Mathematical Founda=
tion:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Number of combinations c=E1=BB=
=A7a r objects from n objects =3D C(n,r) =3D n!/(r!(n-r)!)</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Why This Formula Works:<=
/strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Start v=E1=BB=9Bi permutations:=
 n!/(n-r)! ways to arrange r items from n</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">But we don't care v=E1=BB=81 or=
der c=E1=BB=A7a r items</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Divide by r! to remove ordering=
 variations</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Result: n!/(r!(n-r)!)</li>
</ul>
